# Architecture Rules

## Application Layer

Three Python/FastAPI microservices:

- **User Service** — user management
- **Order Service** — order management; calls Payment Service
- **Payment Service** — payment processing

**Database:** PostgreSQL (shared instance for local development)

## Presentation Layer (Milestone 14)

- **React/Vite frontend** (`frontend/`) — Live Observability Console; local development only
- **Observability BFF** (`services/observability_api/`) — FastAPI read-only curated observability API; local development only
- Browser does **not** query Prometheus, Loki, Tempo, or Alertmanager directly
- Vite dev proxy forwards `/api/users`, `/api/orders`, `/api/payments`, `/api/observability` to local backends
- Reliability catalog pages (`/reliability/services`, `/reliability/slo`, `/reliability/incidents`) are static — not live telemetry
- Live SLO measurements are on `/observability/metrics`, not `/reliability/slo`

## Application Technologies

- Python 3.x
- FastAPI
- Pydantic
- SQLAlchemy
- uv (dependency management)

## Frontend Technologies (Milestone 14)

- React, TypeScript, Vite
- Tailwind CSS, Radix/shadcn-style UI components, Lucide icons

## Infrastructure (introduced progressively)

- Docker
- Docker Compose
- Kubernetes (kind for local development)
- kubectl
- Helm

## CI/CD

- GitHub Actions (backend pytest, Ruff, Docker builds, Helm validation — frontend/BFF not yet in CI)

## Observability (introduced after application deployment)

- Prometheus + PromQL
- Grafana
- Alertmanager
- Loki
- Grafana Alloy
- OpenTelemetry
- Grafana Tempo

Observability backends are deployed in kind via `helm/krp/`. The M14 BFF accesses them via port-forward during local development.

## Runbook Knowledge Assistant (Milestone 15 — planned)

- RAG over repository runbooks and documentation
- `/assistant` UI — currently a placeholder

> A previous roadmap planned separate AI milestones (incident analyzer, tool calling, RAG, remediation as M14–M17). That sequence is superseded. M15 consolidates the next AI layer into the Runbook Knowledge Assistant (RAG).

## Constraints

- Do not introduce additional technologies without explicit approval.
- Do not silently change architecture — explain important decisions.
- Business logic should remain intentionally simple.
- The platform exists to demonstrate operational and reliability engineering concepts.
- Do not claim frontend or BFF are deployed in Kubernetes unless they are added to Helm.
